// Read-only lookups, including the Dorvane approval lookup. Its completed
// response is what the close policy below relies on.
@id("allow_readonly_lookups")
permit (
  principal,
  action in [
    Drupe::Action::"Dorvane___get_approval",
    Drupe::Action::"Kelvora___get_approval",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_failure_codes",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___list_workorders"
  ],
  resource
);

// Closing is allowed only at MAIN, and only if Dorvane (the system of record
// for approvals) returned a completed response within the last hour. That
// response must show an ACCEPTED decision by a PERSON for this exact site and
// work order.
@id("allow_close_with_recent_person_approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Dorvane___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    output.decision: Drupe::decision::"ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: Drupe::approver_kind::"PERSON"
  }
};
```

No policy permits `MaintData___approve_workorder`, so the agent cannot approve work orders. No other mutating tool is permitted either, so there is no indirect route to an approval. Kelvora's approval lookup is allowed as a read-only call, but the close policy never counts it as an approval.

I wrote the `decision` and `approver_kind` values as enum entity literals (`Drupe::decision::"ACCEPTED"`), because the schema declares those fields as enum entities. The reference only shows plain string literals, so if the validator rejects the entity form, swap in `"ACCEPTED"` and `"PERSON"`.

